    "en": "Tyrannosaurus rex was one of the largest meat-eating dinosaurs ever. Adults stretched 11–12 metres and weighed several tonnes. It lived in western North America at the very end of the Cretaceous, alongside Triceratops, and was among the last non-bird dinosaurs before the mass extinction 66 million years ago."
